========================================================================================================================
HPE VM ESSENTIALS (VME) 8.1.2 - MANAGEMENT & COMPUTE NETWORK OPERATIONS
========================================================================================================================

1. MANAGEMENT & COMPUTE BRIDGING TEMPLATE (Save as /etc/netplan/01-netcfg.yaml)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
network:
  version: 2
  renderer: OpenvSwitch
  ethernets:
    eno1:                       # Physical Mgmt Port 1
      dhcp4: no
    eno2:                       # Physical Mgmt Port 2
      dhcp4: no
    ens3f0:                     # Physical Compute Port 1
      dhcp4: no
    ens3f1:                     # Physical Compute Port 2
      dhcp4: no
  bonds:
    bond-mgmt:                  # Management LACP Bond
      interfaces: [eno1, eno2]
      parameters:
        mode: 802.3ad
        mii-monitor-interval: 100
    bond-compute:               # Compute LACP Bond
      interfaces: [ens3f0, ens3f1]
      parameters:
        mode: 802.3ad
        mii-monitor-interval: 100
  ovs-bridges:
    br-mgmt:                    # Local Host Management Bridge
      interfaces: [bond-mgmt]
      addresses: [10.10.10.25/24]
      routes:
        - to: default
          via: 10.10.10.1
    br-compute:                 # VM Compute Core Traffic Bridge
      interfaces: [bond-compute] # Leave unconfigured with IPs on Host OS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. COMPUTE LAYER INTERACTION (virsh / KVM)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KVM Compute Provision  sudo virsh net-define <network_xml_file>        Define an isolated or bridged KVM network
KVM Compute Provision  sudo virsh net-start <network_name>             Power on a defined virtualization network domain
KVM Compute Provision  sudo virsh net-autostart <network_name>         Mark network domain to start instantly on node boot

Network Introspection  sudo virsh net-list --all                       List every guest compute network known to hypervisor
Network Introspection  sudo virsh net-info <network_name>              Output structural metadata of specified bridge domain
Network Introspection  sudo virsh net-dumpxml <network_name>           Export running KVM network infrastructure setup to text
Network Introspection  sudo virsh domiflist <vm_name>                  Map specific VM guest NICs back to host bridge targets

3. INTERACTION & TROUBLESHOOTING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OVS Infrastructure     sudo ovs-vsctl show                             Display running OVS hardware bridges & port layout
OVS Infrastructure     sudo ovs-vsctl list-br                          List text summary of all virtual switch bridges
OVS Infrastructure     sudo ovs-vsctl list-ports <bridge_name>         Show active internal interfaces bound to specific bridge

Data Path Tracking     sudo tcpdump -i br-mgmt -n icmp                 Isolate host management gateway dropouts/ping tests
Data Path Tracking     sudo tcpdump -i br-compute -e                   Listen for tagged 802.1Q trunk traffic on compute
Data Path Tracking     sudo ovs-appctl fdb/show <bridge_name>          Dump OVS physical MAC learning tables per bridge interface
Data Path Tracking     sudo ip link set dev <interface> up             Forcibly wake a dropped network port interface layer
